        "data": {
          "text": "Rank Collapse \u00b7 large orthogonal scale-up (256 samples, 4 classes).\nMechanism: skewed class frequency + bottleneck d=2 + full-batch cross entropy + SGD.\nThis is a synthetic stress test on a larger orthogonal training set; it is not a natural-data reproduction.\nCalibrated (not paper-backed): SGD lr=0.20, rank_aligned_initialization scale=0.30, singularRatio=1.30, random_orthogonal basis. These parameters were selected by a small grid search to obtain a clear warmup -> entropy expansion -> terminal compression signature.\nClass counts: 137/68/34/17 (frequencyRatio=2.0 gives a geometric-like partition, not exact powers of two).\n\nLive generation: the dataset is generated on the fly from the node parameters. You can change inputDim to any value \u2265 4 (e.g., I6, I256, I1024) and trainSize to match it, or switch to rank_orthogonal_scaleup_mse, and the materializer will rebuild the orthogonal sample matrix at runtime; no precomputed artifact is required.",
          "instanceTitle": "Large orthogonal scale-up \u00b7 256 samples"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "rcs-dataset",
        "type": "paper_classification_dataset",
        "position": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 20
        },
        "data": {
